# The screenshots are the artefact you look at; they are not the artefact you
# diff. A full pass writes two PNGs per site per run -- ~10 MB a day, none of it
# reviewable in a patch -- so they stay out of the history and the JSON, the
# table and the per-site serial logs (which ARE diffable, and are what a claim
# gets argued from) stay in.
#
# Re-run the pass if you need the pictures back:
#   make scoreboard-1 SITE=<name>
*.png
*.ppm
net.pcap

# The HOST DOCUMENT is the same trade and was missed when it was added
# (2026-08-20). qmp_site.py fetches each site's HTML with the guest's own
# User-Agent and drops it beside the run, which is how bing's `_w is not
# defined` and stripe's two stacked <h1>s were read -- genuinely useful, and
# genuinely not diffable: 72 files and 18.7 MB after two passes, in a tree
# whose own rules say a commit must be path-limited because another session
# shares the workspace. Burying the real diff under 72 lines of `git status`
# is how the wrong thing gets `git add -A`'d, and these are copies of other
# people's websites.
#
# The reasoning above was already written down, in this file, for the PNGs.
# It was not applied to a new artefact class with the same property.
*.host.html
